{"id":"signal/sigtimedwait","module":"signal","qualname":"sigtimedwait","name":"sigtimedwait","kind":"function","parent":null,"signatures":["sigtimedwait(sigset, timeout)"],"doc":"Like sigwaitinfo(), but takes an additional timeout argument specifying a timeout. If timeout is specified as 0, a poll is performed. Returns None if a timeout occurs.","docsUrl":"https://docs.python.org/3.15/library/signal.html#signal.sigtimedwait","added":"3.3","changed":[{"version":"3.5","text":"The function is now retried with the recomputed timeout if interrupted by a signal not in sigset and the signal handler does not raise an exception (see PEP 475 for the rationale)."},{"version":"3.15","text":"Accepts any real number as timeout, not only integer or float."}],"deprecated":null,"availability":["Unix"],"source":null,"implDetail":false,"isAsync":false},
